<title>ITALY: Gross yields rise at Italian Btp bond auction.</title>
<headline>Gross yields rise at Italian Btp bond auction.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auction results for a seventh tranche of 4.5 trillion lire worth of three-year Italian Treasury fixed rate bonds (Btp) with a 6.00 pct coupon, and a fifth tranche of 4.0 trillion lire of five-year Btps carrying a 6.25 pct coupon.</p>
<p>		  Feb 15, 2000   pvs	March 1, 2002   pvs</p>
<p> Net Yield	 6.64 pct    6.26	  6.80 pct     6.35</p>
<p> Gross Yield     7.43 pct    7.04	  7.67 pct     7.22</p>
<p> Assigned price 96.65	 97.55	 94.80	  96.50</p>
<p> Bids	     9.59 trln lire	   9.61 trln lire</p>
<p> Assigned	 4.50 trln lire	   4.00 trln lire</p>
<p>Note - The comparisons are with a previous auction on March 14 of a fifth tranche of the 3-year paper and a third tranche of five-year BTPs.</p>
</text>
